#X text 240 83 Two-channel equal power panner. The center reduction
is about 3dB. With linear panning ([pan.lin~]) \, the signal level
decreases as it approaches the center using a straight line from ±1
(left or right) to 0 (center) \, resulting in a 6dB reduction in the
middle.;
#X text 240 168 A problem inherent to linear panning is that the perceived
volume of the signal drops in the middle. [pan.sqrt~] solves this.;
